 " gives up to ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1344b5a4-048e-4a60-85dc-e291f0b20ace"],
 " gives every arc."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"1c85d4b4-71bb-4453-8b2b-a53cf262a725"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: with ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " = ",
 StyleBox["d(c, p)", "TI"],
 ", the band ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " is the shell ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], ":", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51d0adf6-66c0-41d8-ac99-c5b409e150ea"],
 ", widened by ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<RadiusDelta\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "863ee38a-49bb-48d6-87a1-833ae9b3898d"],
 ". A minor arc from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " is a shortest path from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " in the subgraph induced on ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 ". A circle through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is a shortest cycle of that subgraph through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " whose removal leaves ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " in a component reaching no further than the band."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"37c1715c-7bc0-409c-af04-9395544e2fb3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["An arc need not exist.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On a lattice a single distance shell has no two adjacent vertices, so the \
bare shell joins no two of its points and the result is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", " ", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6035e713-5158-4107-bbfb-3e19ac6753d7"],
 ". Widening the band fixes it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6775f684-d0b8-4baf-9516-888e93773c95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["An arc need not be unique.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Between two points of a band there are in general many shortest paths, and \
through a point many circles; a trailing count gives them all."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f19b195b-4f9a-4d8c-9af8-39eec9302823"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A polyline reads each piece on the band of its own first point and \
concatenates one arc per piece, so the arcs through an intermediate point are \
the arcs from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " that pass through it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2cda5b35-79fc-4ab4-b6bc-29a0330e0902"],

Cell["\<\
A list that returns to its first point names a closed arc, not a polyline \
there and back. The circles are returned as cyclic vertex lists: the edge \
from the last vertex back to the first is implicit, and the first vertex is \
not repeated.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"93153253-459b-4293-87d0-91b5a68b82b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The search sweeps the band directly: ",
 Cell[BoxData["FindPath"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ad737ada-4534-42ac-b1a8-3b58f87fc5cc"],
 " at the band distance between consecutive points, ",
 Cell[BoxData["FindCycle"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ff35a712-ca5e-485e-8005-b4cbab77c1ca"],
 " length by length for a closed arc. It does not read the graph of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraArc"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraArc", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "191177b9-3c10-4058-870f-e7d5ee6e3fcb"],
 ", so it is the check on that graph. It is the clause ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraRepresentative"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraRepresentative", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9e527cb1-aaa7-42fe-91b4-c0187bbfff4f"],
 " uses for that head; to count arcs without enumerating them, use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2eb457cc-8796-448b-b704-e9cc12916862"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"836aff02-8b1e-46a4-92d5-02d4744b7d90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Option ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<RadiusDelta\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"deltaIn", ",", " ", "deltaOut"}], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cf8a276a-12c7-4453-8116-a72611911aa1"],
 " widens the band to ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["deltaIn", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["d(c, v)", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["deltaOut", "TI"],
 ". A scalar ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<RadiusDelta\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "delta"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23e5682e-3e4d-4e26-bcbf-8ea1b7882403"],
 " means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "delta"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e2724e92-08f1-4c2a-9a83-915af402cbb0"],
 ", outward only. The default is ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ebe1a78d-e4c2-478f-9c0d-00ed3f8a5383"],
 ". There is no ",
 Cell[BoxData["Method"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9fac890e-aa8c-4375-aef8-ad31967dea5c"],
 " and no ",
 Cell[BoxData["Properties"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44899b1c-2967-40c3-a33f-51dbc8a0c103"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3d461215-a6e7-4efb-bd4e-22fd14e5d3b3"]
}, Open  ]],

